  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed roof extension over the outrigger due to its excessive size and unsympathetic design would detract from the character and appearance of the host building and would fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Merton (John Innes - Wilton Crescent) Conservation Area. As such, the proposal would fail to comply with Policies HC1 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies D12.3, D12.4 and D12.5 of the Merton Local Plan 2024.  ",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed roof extension over the outrigger would extend to far out and would appear overbearing to the occupants of the host building and the neighbours when in their rear gardens to the detriment of amenity. As such, the proposal would fail to comply with Policy D12.3 of the Merton Local Plan 2024.  ",
    "Reason : 3 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance: \r\n\"\tThe application was considered to be fundamentally contrary to the provisions of the Development Plan and the NPPF, and there were not considered to be any solutions to resolve this conflict. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
  ],
